  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohammed Azarudeen vs / on 20 March, 2024 Author: Sathi Kumar Sukumara Kurup Bench: Sathi Kumar Sukumara Kurup Wp(Md) Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 20.03.2024 Coram: The Honourable Mr.Justice Sathi Kumar Sukumara Kurup W.P.(Md) No.6737 of 2024 Mohammed Azarudeen ... Peti /vs./ 1.The Commissioner of Police, Madurai City, Madurai. 2.The Inspector of Police, Mattuthavani Police Station, Madurai. ... Resp Prayer: Writ Petition filed under Article 226 of the Constitution of Ind issuance of Writ of Mandamus, to forbear the Respondents herein from interfering with the Petitioner's peaceful running of his hotel/eatery i of ''Azar Biriyani'' functioning at 24, Fruit Market Complex, Mattuthava Melur Main Road, Madurai during late night hours. For Petitioner : Mr.K.Bharathi For Respondents : Mr.B.Thanga Aravindh Government Advocate (Criminal https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis 1/8 Wp(Md) No Order Mohammed Azarudeen vs / on 20 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/93100143/",
    "facts": "Since the respondents did not take any action, the petitioner approached this Court by way of filing this petition.",
    "arguments": "According to the petitioner, the said eatery shop is his only source of income and maximum customers used to visit his shop only during the mid night hours. Therefore, the act of the respondents in insisting the petitioner to close the shop by 10.30 p.m. causes great inconvenience to him and also to many customers, who regularly come to his shop for dinner from various quarters of life. 5. The learned Government Advocate (Criminal Side) submitted that there is violation of G.O.Ms.No.61 Labour Welfare and Skill Development (K2) dated 02.06.2022. For violation of the said Government Order, it is for the authorities under the Shops and Establishments Act to pass appropriate orders https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis even sealing the shop of the Petitioner."
  },
